      "description": "Watch West Ham vs Wolverhampton highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 1, 2026. The stadium was buzzing with anticipation as the sides took to the pitch for this pivotal Championship clash on September 1, 2026 . High-Octane First Half The game exploded into life early on, with both sides trading blows in a display of attacking football. Divine Mukasa drew first blood for West Ham in the 33rd minute, clinical finishing following an assist from Arne Engels . The momentum continued to favor the hosts as Jarrod Bowen stepped up in the 42nd minute to coolly convert a penalty. Just as it seemed West Ham might run away with it, Marshall Munetsi pulled one back for Manchester United in the 44th minute, ensuring a tense finish to the first half. A Dramatic Twist in the Tale The second half saw no shortage of action as Divine Mukasa netted his second goal of the afternoon in the 53rd minute, again assisted by Jarrod Bowen . However, the tide turned in bizarre fashion shortly after. Konstantinos Mavropanos found the net for his side in the 64th minute, only to commit a costly own goal just five minutes later. The closing stages were defined by tactical changes and rising tension, with Jordan James and Valentin Castellanos both entering the referee's book. Despite the frantic push for a late winner, the match ended in a stalemate after the final whistle blew at 90+5 minutes."
